-- title:
--   Descent of a Kummer presentation along étale base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a regular local domain which is complete (more precisely, adically complete) with respect to its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$ and has Krull dimension at most $2$; let $s \in \mathfrak m_R$ with $s \notin \mathfrak m_R^2$, and let $e$ be a positive natural number whose image in $R$ is a unit. Let $R'$ be a local ring which is an $R$-algebra that is finite and free as an $R$-module and étale over $R$, and let $B$ be a noetherian local domain, integrally closed in its fraction field, which is an $R$-algebra finite as an $R$-module and such that $R \to B$ is injective (faithful scalar multiplication). Let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $R$ and $F$ a field that is simultaneously an extension of $K_0$ and a fraction field of $B$, the two $R$-algebra structures being compatible, with $\dim_{K_0} F = e$. Assume further that $B$ is residually generated by $R$ in the weak sense that every $b \in B$ satisfies $b - \mathrm{alg\,map}(r) \in \mathfrak m_B$ for some $r \in R$, and that for some unit $u' \in (R')^\times$ there is an isomorphism of $R'$-algebras $R' \otimes_R B \cong R'[X]/(X^e - u's)$. Then there exists a unit $u \in R^\times$ and an isomorphism of $R$-algebras $B \cong R[X]/(X^e - us)$.
--
--   This is the descent step for Kummer presentations: an isomorphism of the base change $R' \otimes_R B$ with a standard $e$-th root extension of $R'$, obtained over a finite étale local cover $R'$, is converted into such a presentation of $B$ itself over $R$, at the cost of changing the unit multiplying $s$. It is used in the analysis of cyclic covers unramified outside the divisor $s = 0$, feeding [`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_algEquiv_adjoinRoot_X_pow_sub_C_mul_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue`](thm.html#IsRegularLocalRing.exists_algEquiv_adjoinRoot_X_pow_sub_C_mul_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue).
